  "details": "Since I've used persona before to verify my identity for twitch affiliation I got kinda surprised that it let me pick a previously taken photo of my ID instead of requiring me to take a fresh one for VRC age verification\n\nI see a potential abuse in this, as persona doesnt have access to government databases, and cannot verify the legitimacy of the ID aside from just verifying that it looks like a gov-issued ID should look like. Even though it does require a selfie liveness check, nothing stops anyone from using an ID and photoshopping/using an ID of someone with alike face\n\nAnd given that in the new flow you don't keep any data, you have no practical way of looking back at it manually and verifying that ID, was, in fact, legit.\n\nHence I think it'd only make sense to disable this feature to reduce the fraud percentage as much as possible. Requiring to take a photo instead of letting uploading one is less convenient, but I'd rather be sure that a person with 18+ badge is actually 18+ and not someone who photoshopped their passport from 2008 to 2004",
